Shades are a special case. If your weapon is made of silver, it
behaves normally. Otherwise, the base damage for the weapon
(Sdam,Ldam) is ZERO, and the weapon's plus does NOT add (but neither
does the rusting penalty). However, if your weapon is blessed, you
still inflict the +d4 damage. Also, if your weapon is made of Silver,
the silver bonus (+d20) still applies. Bonuses for Strength still seem
to apply, as well. This is why Shades seem to be so hard to kill.

